// [Basis] Attributes should be listed in group order (0–10), and within each group, static attributes should be listed in the order of static → dynamic attributes.
// For group definitions, see PLAN.md "HTML/Vue/JSX/Svelte Attribute Order Rule".
//
// Target: .jsx / .tsx (JSX) only. See "Vue / Svelte / HTML" note below.
//
// Reference: https://vuejs.org/style-guide/rules-recommended.html#element-attribute-order
//
// [Implementation notes]
// 1. A bare metavariable (`id=$id`) cannot bind to a JSX attribute value in this
//    Biome/GritQL engine — neither a string literal (`id="x"`) nor an expression
//    container (`id={x}`) matches. Only a fully literal value, or `{$expr}` against an
//    already-expression-valued attribute, binds successfully. Attribute-order checks
//    therefore cannot be written as `<$tag a=$a b=$b>` snippets.
// 2. `contains` combined with an `as`-bound node-type pattern (`JsxOpeningElement()`,
//    `JsxSelfClosingElement()`) only ever reports the first match in the file — later
//    matches are silently dropped. Likewise, patterns inside `sequential { }` need an
//    explicit `bubble` to avoid the same single-match collapse, but `bubble` did not
//    fix the `contains` case either. Using the node-type pattern directly at the top
//    level (no `contains`) auto-bubbles per match and reports every element.
// 3. `$el <: r"..."` requires the regex to match the ENTIRE node text, not a substring
//    search — patterns must be wrapped in `.*...*.` (see no-null-type.grit for the same
//    pattern). This also means order checks can compare text position of two attribute
//    names directly, which incidentally lifts the old "adjacent pairs only" limitation:
//    a `.*first.*second.*` regex catches out-of-order attributes even when unrelated
//    attributes sit between them.
// 4. Multiple independent checks against the same matched element must be combined with
//    `any { }` (all branches run), not `or { }` (first match wins) or `sequential { }`
//    (designed for staged rewrites over `file($body)`, not independent scans).
//
// [Vue / Svelte / HTML — currently out of scope]
// GritQL plugins in this Biome version only compile snippets against JavaScript/TypeScript
// (including JSX), CSS, and JSON syntax trees. A `.vue` SFC's `<script>` block is JS/TS and
// can be targeted (see enforce-pure-src.grit), but its `<template>` block is not — no
// `language` directive (html, vue, ...) makes GritQL patterns match template markup, so a
// Vue/Svelte/HTML version of this rule cannot be implemented today. Revisit once Biome's
// GritQL plugin support extends to template languages.

engine biome(1.0)
language js(typescript, jsx)

or {
  JsxSelfClosingElement(),
  JsxOpeningElement()
} as $el where {
  any {
    // Group 0 (key) → Group 1 (id)
    //
    // ✗  <Item id="x" key={k} />
    // ✓  <Item key={k} id="x" />
    $el <: r".*\bid\s*=.*\bkey\s*=.*" where {
      register_diagnostic(span=$el, message="[Attribute Order Rule] The `key` (Group 0) should be written before the `id` (Group 1).", severity="warn")
    },
    // Group 1 (id) → Group 3 (className)
    //
    // ✗  <div className="foo" id="bar" />
    // ✓  <div id="bar" className="foo" />
    $el <: r".*\bclassName\s*=.*\bid\s*=.*" where {
      register_diagnostic(span=$el, message="[Attribute Order Rule] The `id` (Group 1) should be written before the `className` (Group 3).", severity="warn")
    },
    // Group 3 (className) → Group 8 (aria-*)
    //
    // ✗  <div aria-label="..." className="..." />
    // ✓  <div className="..." aria-label="..." />
    $el <: r".*\baria-[\w-]+\s*=.*\bclassName\s*=.*" where {
      register_diagnostic(span=$el, message="[Attribute Order Rule] `aria-*` (Group 8: Accessibility) should be written after `className` (Group 3).", severity="warn")
    },
    // Group 3 (className) → Group 9 (data-*)
    //
    // ✗  <div data-testid="..." className="..." />
    // ✓  <div className="..." data-testid="..." />
    $el <: r".*\bdata-[\w-]+\s*=.*\bclassName\s*=.*" where {
      register_diagnostic(span=$el, message="[Attribute Order Rule] `data-*` (Group 9: data attribute) should be written after `className` (Group 3).", severity="warn")
    },
    // Group 3 (className) → Group 10 (on*)
    //
    // ✗  <Button onClick={fn} className="..." />
    // ✓  <Button className="..." onClick={fn} />
    $el <: r".*\bon[A-Z]\w*\s*=.*\bclassName\s*=.*" where {
      register_diagnostic(span=$el, message="[Attribute Order Rule] `on*` (Group 10: Event) should be written after `className` (Group 3).", severity="warn")
    },
    // Group 1 (id) → Group 10 (on*)
    //
    // ✗  <Button onClick={fn} id="btn" />
    // ✓  <Button id="btn" onClick={fn} />
    $el <: r".*\bon[A-Z]\w*\s*=.*\bid\s*=.*" where {
      register_diagnostic(span=$el, message="[Attribute Order Rule] `on*` (Group 10: Event) should be written after `id` (Group 1).", severity="warn")
    }
  }
}
